{\plain {Here is an example of what the 
estimate for the coefficient looks like.
  We had to define a new temp demodulation
 using the absolute value of s}{\fs16 \dn6 
n,k}{\fs16  }{\fs20 because Mathcad picks
 a new digital sequence every}{\fs16 \dn6 
 \par }{\fs20 time you open this file. By
 doing this, we have altered the amplitude
 of the estimated coefficient.  The correct
 amplitude should be near +1 and -1 for 
logics 1 and 0 respectively.  However, the
 graphs still illustrate that the estimate
 coeffecient for logic 1 should be positive
 and that for logic 0 should be negative.}}
}
