.TXT 20 2 262 0
Cg a66.900000,67.000000,682
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
{\f1\fnil Symbol;}
}
{\plain {\b \fs16 Again, in the above analysis
 we had to use the temp demodulation defined
 in the }{\b \ul \fs16 Detection/Demodulation}{\b 
\fs16  section }{\b \fs16 because Mathcad
 picks a new sequence everytime you open
 the file. As a result, the y-axis scale
 of the above graphs is wrong but, the graphs
 still show that a local oscillator error
 will cause an error in the estimate for
 the coefficient. Specificly, the magnitude
 of the coeffecient is less than it should
 be in the above graphs.  The correct values
 for the real estimate will be close to 
-1 for logic 0 and close to 1 for logic 
1.  And, the errored estimates will be very
 close to zero as is shown on the graphs
 above.}}
}
